<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76799" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰλαί-φᾰτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φημί</span>) poet. Adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			<i>spoken long ago</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ μάλα δή με π. θέσφαθ᾽ ἱκάνει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.507
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				2.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				454
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. λόγος, ἀραί</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				750
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				766
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>spoken of long ago, legendary</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρῦς
				π.</span> an oak <i>of ancient story</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.163
			</span></i> (vv. ll. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παλαίφαγος,
			παλαίφυτος</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>of ancient fame, made known</i> or <i>declared of old</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενεά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					6.31
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					532
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόνοια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					823
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δίκη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OC</u>
					1381
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχάρναι δὲ παλαίφατον
			εὐάνορες</span> Acharnae was brave <i>of old time</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				2.16
			</span></i>.</div>
